## 3. HOMEPAGE ARCHITECTURE (`index.html`)

`index.html` is a **single-file multi-page app** using hash routing:

- Each "page" is `<div class="ao-page" id="page-<name>">`. Only `.active` is displayed.
- Pages: `home`, `careers`, `contact`, `lander`, `statefarm`, `allstate`, `acquire`, `enthusiast`, `swag`.
- `navigate('<name>')` switches pages, sets `location.hash`, highlights the nav link with `data-page`. On load, the hash (default `home`) picks the page.
- Nav links use `onclick="navigate('x');aoCloseNav()" href="#x" data-page="x"`.
- **To add a homepage page:** add a `.ao-page` div with `id="page-<name>"`, add a nav link, done. Keep it inside the one file.
- Mobile nav toggles `.ao-nav-links.open`.

### Conversion tracking (keep intact)
- `window.trackEvent(eventName, buttonId)` logs to `gtag` (if present), to `localStorage['ao_conversions']` (last 100), console, and a `sendBeacon('/track')` (no backend; harmless).
- Page views go to `localStorage['ao_pageviews']`.
- CTA button IDs are stable identifiers used by the dashboard: `hero_cta`, `urgency_cta`, `pain_cta`, `proof_cta`, `offer_cta`, `final_cta`, `phone_cta`. Do not rename. Add new CTAs with `onclick="trackEvent('cta_click','<new_id>')"`.

### Scarcity band
- Month names come from the real date in JS. Spot counts come from `monthly-config.json` (fetched with cache-busting), and only apply when `currentMonth`/`currentYear` match today; otherwise the page falls back to 3. **The only monthly edit is that JSON file.**

### A/B headline testing
- Variants live in `.claude/ab_test_config.json`. To switch, replace the `<h1 class="ao-h1">` text in `#page-home` and commit `"A/B Test: Activate Variant B headline"`. Change one thing at a time; run a week; 100+ visitors minimum before calling a winner.

### Swag page
- Fetches `/swag-products.json` at runtime. Products come from Printify shop `27019610` via the GitHub Action. Edit the Action's transform step, not the JSON.

### Structured data
- Homepage has `LocalBusiness` (telephone, address, areaServed, openingHours, priceRange) and `FAQPage` JSON-LD. Keep valid JSON. City pages and the cost guide have their own schema; mirror the pattern on new SEO pages.

